NAME
    framelog - sample a memory value once per frame

SYNOPSIS
    framelog add <space> <addr> [<width>]
    framelog list
    framelog show <id> [<count>]
    framelog clear <id>
    framelog remove <id>

DESCRIPTION
    Records the value at hex address <addr> in memory space <space> once
    per frame, regardless of whether any instruction read or wrote it.
    Unlike watch(1), which fires only on memory accesses, 'framelog'
    captures a continuous per-frame timeline of a value.

OPTIONS
    add <space> <addr> [<width>]
        Register a per-frame sampler at <addr> in <space> with byte width
        1, 2, or 4 (default 1, little-endian).

    list
        List active frame logs with their IDs, spaces, addresses, widths,
        and sample counts.

    show <id> [<count>]
        Print up to <count> recorded (frame, value) samples for frame log
        #<id> (default 20).

    clear <id>
        Discard stored samples for frame log #<id> without removing it.

    remove <id>
        Remove frame log #<id>.

EXAMPLES
    framelog add WRAM 1fb0 2
    framelog list
    framelog show 1 50
    framelog remove 1

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage/not-found message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid argument, or session
        service fault.

SEE ALSO
    watch(1), counters(1), mem(1), spaces(1)
